```java
import org.jsoup.Jsoup;
import org.jsoup.nodes.Document;
import org.jsoup.nodes.Comment;

public class GeneratedData {

    @org.junit.Test
    public void testGeneratedComments() {
        // Create a new Document object
        Document document = Jsoup.parse("<data>Hello World!</data>");

        // Generate an HTML comment using the createComment() method
        Comment comment = document.createComment("This is a generated comment");

        // Print the contents of the comment
        System.out.println(comment.data());

        // Extract the data from the document using the select() method
        String originalData = document.select("data").first().text();

        assertEquals(originalData, "Hello World!");
    }
    
    public class Comment {
        private String data;

        public Comment(String data) {
            this.data = data;
        }

        public String getData() {
            return data;
        }

        @Override
        public String toString() {
            return "<!-- " + data + " -->";
        }
    }
}
```

This example creates a new `Document` object and parses an HTML string. It then generates an HTML comment using the `createComment()` method, prints its contents to the console, extracts the data from the document using the `select()` method, and checks if it matches the expected value.

Note that this is just a simple example to demonstrate how to generate data in Java using Jsoup for generating HTML comments. The actual implementation may vary depending on your specific requirements.
